    </DisplayTable>




<p>The Lewis form factor <InlineEquation equation="Y" /> accounts for tooth geometry and depends on the number of teeth and pressure angle. Larger numbers of teeth increase <InlineEquation equation="Y" />, reducing bending stress. Typical values range from <InlineEquation equation="0.2 < Y < 0.5" />.</p>
<p>A more refined stress model incorporates real-world effects:</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="\\sigma = \\frac{F_t P}{bJ} K_v K_o K_m" title="" />

<p>Gear teeth experience cyclic loading, leading to fatigue failure at the root.</p>

<DisplayEquation equation="S_n = S_n' C_L C_G C_s k_r k_t k_{ms}" title="" />

